# @extern rejects ambiguous
# ABI HAZARD, NOW REFUSED. Zebra `int` is i64. C `int` is 32-bit. So
# `extern def f(n: int)` against a C `int` parameter is an ABI MISMATCH THAT LINKS
# CLEANLY and corrupts the stack.
#
# This probe was written as `accepts` against decision A of docs/extern_ffi_design.md
# ("the compiler cannot know which C type is meant") with the note that a later
# warning would fail it and be the signal to rewrite it. BUG-270 (2026-08-06) did
# exactly that: `int` in an extern signature is refused, naming `int32`/`int64`.
# Rewritten 2026-09-16 when the runner lost its bootstrap leg and the red was read.
extern def zebra_probe_wide(n: int): int

def main()
    print("declared")
